    "message": "fix(mcp): harden the stdio server — line-size cap, tree-kill, protocol-abuse matrix (#219)\r\n\r\n- Byte-bounded line reader replaces readline: a message over 1 MiB is\r\n  rejected with -32700 and the reader resyncs at the next newline, so a\r\n  pathological client can never force unbounded buffering.\r\n- Reject JSON-RPC batches with a single -32600; validate jsonrpc version\r\n  and id type per JSON-RPC 2.0.\r\n- Kill whole process trees on cancel/timeout/overflow/shutdown: children\r\n  spawn detached (own group on POSIX; taskkill /T on Windows), and the\r\n  executor tracks live children for disposeAll() on EOF and SIGINT/SIGTERM,\r\n  so a tool that spawned the indexing backend cannot leak it.\r\n- 14 new tests: protocol-abuse matrix (oversize, batch, malformed shapes,\r\n  unknown _meta, concurrent cancels, sequential queue, notification storm,\r\n  idempotent initialize, partial frame at EOF) + grandchild reaping and\r\n  disposeAll() orphan-prevention. Full suite 749 passed / 2 skipped.",
